{
  "version": "predicates-v10",
  "description": "Predicates a ProposalDraft may use. Wikidata mappings say which source statements can evidence each predicate: forward means the statement's entity is the assertion subject; inverse means the statement's value is the assertion subject. v2: commanded relates a person to a force (Group), not to an event. v3: authority held over a force (heldAuthorityOver) is separated from command actually exercised (commanded); evidence for one never counts for the other. v4: each predicate declares its qualifiers (context, role, time: none, optional, required, or withRole for time required only when a role is given) and its claim modes; adds the unary occurred and authorOf (22-CLAIM-QUALIFIERS.md). v5: each predicate declares a category (factual or interpretive); kinds Office and Concept; narrative links triggeredBy and resultedIn; interpretive exemplifies and ledTo (attributed only) and depictsSameAs (curator) (23-NARRATIVE-AND-NOTES.md). v6: occurred extends to Period (each source's bounds an attributed claim); subperiodOf and followedBy relate periods; partOf stays Event to Event (24-PERIODS-AND-TRANSFORMATION.md). v7: opposed relates people or groups who were opponents, symmetric, time required, with an optional context event (the war or battle); political, military, or personal opposition is not split. Works carry a form; a claim attributed to a Work of a creative form is imaginative, derived and never chosen (25-LIVES-AND-PLAYGROUND.md section 6). v8: born and died are dated unary claims (no date is a bare property; 25 section 10), from Wikidata P569 and P570; participatedIn also maps P1344 (participant in). v9 (2026-10-13; docs/Response - Roman Republican Institutions and Military Hierarchies.md): kinds Type (unit types, organizational patterns, roles, powers) and Polity (states); partOf extended to Groups and Types, its endpoint kinds paired (kindPairs) so an event is never part of a group; instanceOf, precedes, electedBy, exercisedPower, heldPower, servedUnder, memberOf; a quantity qualifier (minimum, maximum, typical) on partOf and electedBy; context and role kinds per predicate (contextKinds, roleKinds; defaults Event and the roleKind). P361 on a Person and P463 map to memberOf; which predicate a P361 statement evidences follows from its endpoints' kinds. Facts that happen once (once: true: born, died, occurred, bornAt, diedAt, occurredAt) are disputed when their sources give different times, places, contexts, or roles; any other fact may recur (two consulships, two marriages), so such differences are separate occasions, not a dispute. occurred extended to Polity: a state's existence, by each source's dates. v10 (2026-10-15; 29-EVENT-CENTRED-INQUIRY.md, 23-NARRATIVE-AND-NOTES.md section 2): happenedBefore orders events as a source narrates them (Event to Event, no time: the order itself is the content); it is separate from precedes, the dated order of offices. occurred takes an optional context event, so a depicted event's time marker can be anchored to the event it happens within (a relative offset).",
